{"id":"hist-gfc-2008","title":"2008 Global Financial Crisis","source":"historical","difficulty":"hard","generator":"yahoo-finance","storyline":"The US housing bust turns into a global banking crisis. Lehman Brothers fails in September 2008, credit markets freeze and equities halve before unprecedented central-bank and government action finds a floor in March 2009.","regime":{"name":"Credit stress building","description":"Housing is falling, banks are writing down mortgage assets and funding markets are tense. Oil is near record highs.","factorDrift":{},"volMult":1},"events":[{"id":"h1","t":0.1961,"date":"2008-07-11","headline":"IndyMac seized by regulators; oil hits record $147","altHeadline":"Large US mortgage lender seized by regulators as oil hits a record high","body":"It is one of the largest bank failures in US history. Depositors queued outside branches.","source":"wire","category":"credit","magnitude":"moderate","sentiment":-1,"kind":"normal","factorShocks":{}},{"id":"h2","t":0.3569,"date":"2008-09-08","headline":"US Treasury takes over Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac","altHeadline":"US government takes control of the two giant mortgage-finance agencies","body":"The agencies own or guarantee about half of all US mortgages. Shareholders are largely wiped out.","source":"wire","category":"credit","magnitude":"major","sentiment":-1,"kind":"normal","factorShocks":{}},{"id":"h3","t":0.3765,"date":"2008-09-15","headline":"Lehman Brothers files for bankruptcy; Merrill Lynch sold to Bank of America","altHeadline":"A major Wall Street investment bank files for bankruptcy; a rival is sold in a rescue deal","body":"No government rescue was offered. Counterparties around the world are scrambling to assess their exposure.","source":"wire","category":"credit","magnitude":"major","sentiment":-1,"kind":"normal","factorShocks":{}},{"id":"h4","t":0.3843,"date":"2008-09-17","headline":"Fed rescues AIG with $85bn loan; money-market fund \"breaks the buck\"","altHeadline":"Fed rescues the world's largest insurer; a money-market fund falls below $1 a share","body":"Investors are pulling cash from money funds and short-term lending between banks has frozen.","source":"central_bank","category":"credit","magnitude":"moderate","sentiment":-1,"kind":"normal","factorShocks":{}},{"id":"h5","t":0.4157,"date":"2008-09-29","headline":"US House rejects $700bn bank bailout plan","altHeadline":"US lawmakers vote down the $700bn bank rescue plan","body":"The surprise defeat removes the backstop markets had been counting on.","source":"wire","category":"geopolitics","magnitude":"major","sentiment":-1,"kind":"normal","factorShocks":{}},{"id":"h6","t":0.4431,"date":"2008-10-08","headline":"Fed, ECB, BoE and others cut rates together in emergency move","altHeadline":"Major central banks cut rates together in a co-ordinated emergency move","body":"Each bank lowered its policy rate by 50bp. China also cut rates.","source":"central_bank","category":"central_bank","magnitude":"major","sentiment":1,"kind":"normal","factorShocks":{}},{"id":"h7","t":0.5333,"date":"2008-11-10","headline":"China announces RMB 4 trillion stimulus package","altHeadline":"Beijing announces a giant stimulus package worth about 13% of GDP","body":"Spending will focus on infrastructure, housing and rural development over two years.","source":"wire","category":"china_policy","magnitude":"major","sentiment":1,"kind":"normal","factorShocks":{}},{"id":"h8","t":0.6353,"date":"2008-12-16","headline":"Fed cuts rates to 0-0.25% and promises to buy bonds","altHeadline":"Fed cuts rates to near zero and promises large-scale bond purchases","body":"The Fed said rates will stay exceptionally low \"for some time\".","source":"central_bank","category":"central_bank","magnitude":"major","sentiment":1,"kind":"normal","factorShocks":{}},{"id":"h9","t":0.7843,"date":"2009-02-10","headline":"Geithner's bank rescue plan disappoints: few details","altHeadline":"New US Treasury chief's bank rescue plan lacks detail; 